target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestStdinIsReadOnlyWhenAskedFor/an_idle_pipe'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    stdin is read only under `-findings-file -`. The earlier rule, the Python's, read it whenever it was not a terminal, and an inherited pipe nobody writes to is not a terminal: on 2026-10-11 an orchestrator flushing a report by hand ran `looper pr-report --post` with its harness's stdin, and it sat silent for minutes until killed. This restores the implicit read; the test hands it an idle pipe and fails on the timeout instead of hanging.
--- old
	if path == "" {
		return "", nil
	}
--- new
	if path == "" {
		path = "-"
	}
